$ goodfetch-collie run start --help
Starts a Run its program drives, and answers once it is started. A Run ID names the Run for good: a start with an existing Run ID returns that Run as it is when the caller and the inputs match, and fails with `run_conflict` otherwise

Usage: goodfetch-collie run start [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --project <PROJECT>  The project configuration the Client found, layer 3 (ADR 0083)
      --run-id <RUN_ID>    The Run's ID; the engine generates a lowercase ULID when it is absent. An existing ID returns that Run when the caller and the inputs match, and fails with `run_conflict` otherwise
      --set <KEY=VALUE>    Sets a setting for this run, as `key=value`, the value read as JSON when it parses as JSON and as text otherwise, a duration as milliseconds or as `45s`, `2m` or `1h`; repeatable
      --settings <FILE|->  Reads settings for this run from a JSON object, nested by key, in FILE, or from standard input for `-`; `--set` beats it
      --tags <TAGS>        The Run's opaque tags
      --json               Prints the result as JSON
      --color <WHEN>       When to colour human output; `auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set and not empty [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help               Print help

$ goodfetch-collie run finish --help
