$ goodfetch-collie run abort --help
Stops a Run at its next safe point, `stopped` and `incomplete`: no attempt in flight commits, and its work items return to pending. Answers its Run report; an ended Run's report is answered as it is. A Run whose engine died is stopped by this engine, which takes its writer role at the next run epoch; a Run another engine writes is stopped by that engine, the owner the Run index names

Usage: goodfetch-collie run abort [OPTIONS] <RUN_ID>

Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>  The Run's ID

Options:
      --forwarded     Set by an engine that forwards the abort to the owner the Run index names (ADR 0031): an engine that does not own the Run then answers `run_not_owned` instead of taking its writer role
      --json          Prints the result as JSON
      --color <WHEN>  When to colour human output; `auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set and not empty [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -h, --help          Print help

